  "body": "Track current pixel density and EXIF dimensions per image request\n\n`current pixel density` and `preferred density-corrected dimensions` describe a fetched image, but they are stored on the `img` element. Once an `img` has both a `current request` on screen and a `pending request` loading, one per-element slot can't serve both:\n\n- A new `pending request` overwrites the density of the image still being shown, changing `naturalWidth`/`naturalHeight` before the new image is available (#5607).\n- Re-selecting a `partially available` URL at a new density returns early without updating it, so the image loads with the stale density; browsers already update it (#13049).\n- `density-corrected natural width and height` mutates the stored EXIF dimensions on every read, and they are never cleared, so a later non-EXIF image inherits them.\n- `last selected source` is only recorded without `srcset`/`picture`, so in responsive mode every environment change re-fetches the same source (#5060).\n\nThis moves both fields onto `image request` and keeps them in sync in the selection algorithms:\n\n- Set `current pixel density` when an `image request` is created or taken from the `list of available images`; update it on the `current request` (clearing any `pending request`) or `pending request` when their URL is re-selected at a new density.\n- Make `density-corrected natural width and height` return a fresh width/height pair, and reset the stored dimensions when a request is aborted or prepared for presentation.\n- Record `last selected source` whenever a source is selected, and reset it (with density 1) when nothing is selected, so `react to changes in the environment` only fetches on a real change.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64903.\n\nFixes #5060.\nFixes #5607.\nFixes #13049.\n\n---\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (already implements #5060 and #13049; #5607 pending)\n   * Gecko (already implements #5060 and #13049; #5607 pending)\n   * WebKit (already implements #5060 and #13049; #5607 pending)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64903\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/584147744\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2091380\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=330918\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): N/A\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): N/A\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13210/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 1:00 PM UTC (cf99394)\">/images.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13210/5fcc231...cf99394/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on N